	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg11598"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=765" title="View the profile of Moraganna">Moraganna</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Female.gif" alt="Female" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 23<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/ceres.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								Kiss muh cute ass~<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=765"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1160.msg11598#msg11598"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1160.msg11598#msg11598">Re: Parents.. a little help plz..</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #37 on:</b> October 06, 2004, 08:37:01 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Ohhh I just found this hehe. I have two girls, my oldest used to take her diaper off too. Yeah I know how annoying it is to walk up on your child bear bottom peeing or pooping on the floor when they where supposed to be asleep. I would lay her down and same as you I would do house chores because we all for god sakes know you can&#039;t do a damn thing when the kids are up. So after a month or so of this I decided to try pull ups. It was so hot out I didn&#039;t want to stack clothes on her. Plus she would just take her clothes off anyways. So I tried pull ups and they worked, yes they are a little more expensive but compared to the cleaners you are useing to clean up the stains ... they are nothing. My lil one is just over 1 and I started the pull up&#039;s early just to avoid this problem from even happening. Once she learned to take the velcro off her diapers I knew it was time.<br /><br />As for being able to watch your kids every wakeing hour, it just isn&#039;t possible. Unless you like to live in a messy home. But then you would have someone saying omg those kids are neglected look at the house they live in take them away. In todays time parents are damned if they do and damned if they don&#039;t. So until you have kids I suggest you keep your suggestions to yourself. Being a parent is not as easy as it looks. 
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
