								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1160.msg11602#msg11602">Re: Parents.. a little help plz..</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #38 on:</b> October 06, 2004, 02:35:08 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1160.msg11475#msg11475">Quote from: Dwalion SoulVoid on September 29, 2004, 02:48:26 pm</a></div><div class="quote">In all seriousness, do the following<br />1.  Change diaper more frequently.<br />2.  Do not leave child unattended for excessive durations.<br />3.  Learn the fuck to log off Everquest.<br /><br /><br />The thing is, shit and urine burns and/or is just plain uncomfortable after being left on the sensitive area, buttocks or genitalia.  Since your child, like mine, are probably human beings, that is not something normally desired.  So they begin to remove the undesired by product, then out of curiosity and/or sheer boredom, they realize that applying it to the walls is not only fun, but a good way to go back and old dad or mom for ignoring them, and more than likely without even knowing!<br /><br />If you are unable to meet these suggestions, hire a Nanny, have someone&#039;s mother watch them or give them up for adoption.<br /><br />It really fucking bothers me when shit like this happens.<br /></div><br />My favorite suggestions are # 2 and #3…<br /><br />This coming from a member of one of the top 3 guilds on RN!&nbsp; <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/cool.gif" alt="Cool" border="0" /><br /><br />Apology or not, you have no idea what your talking about. Kids get curious champ and that’s how some of them express it. My daughter did it once while we thought she was taking nap. Well before EQ was released.<br />
						</td>
					</tr>
