							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1160.msg11610#msg11610"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1160.msg11610#msg11610">Re: Parents.. a little help plz..</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #39 on:</b> October 07, 2004, 03:06:22 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I will show some sympathy for the unaware.<br /><br />Moraganna, if your comment was directed at me, I stated before, I have three children.<br />(Two children stay with their mother, from previous marriage.)<br /><br />Ldian, since you directly qouted me, then allow me correct you directly.<br /><br />Arirang hasn&#039;t been in the top three of anything as per the populace of eqvault or this board in almost a year.&nbsp; There are three people who log on from time to time, including me.&nbsp; <br /><br />While raiding with Arirang, my wife and I would take turns tending to the child.&nbsp; At the time when I applied I worked from 7pm til 3-5am, logged on, got the scoop, woke my wife, whom is a stay at home mother/wife, her day began as mine wound down.&nbsp; We managed to raise our daughter thus far in what I consider a loving and meaningful way.<br /><br />I did apologize, however, to you it did not matter, and probably did not matter to the original poster or hell, anyone for that matter.&nbsp; I am not going to attempt to rehash what I said, just understand this, I saw the post for what I thought it was and in the best interest of myself and those who were offended, I made an apology.&nbsp; <br /><br />Obviously I learned that some parents can have children who explore into their diapers and not be the result of some sort of neglect or abuse.<br /><br />It is also important that for those of you who are reading this to understand, I am very protective of my children and for those children who in my opinion are in harms way.&nbsp; I can say that I personally am thankful I aired my opinion of what the original poster stated vice calling HRS on him, (provided I knew his RL information) because that would of been a mistake.<br /><br />Or I could of just summed up this by saying, Yes, I am a mean, bull headed son-of-a-bitch.&nbsp; Take a number, my wife gets first dibs.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />Dwalion SoulVoid &lt;Arirang&gt;<br />70 Necromancer <br /><br />You will more than likely post something stupid and I will respond with something witty.&nbsp; I will more than likely post something stupid and you will respond with something witty.
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg11613"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=745" title="View the profile of Needaa">Needaa</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Female.gif" alt="Female" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 32<br />
								<br />
								<br />
								
								
								<a href="http://edit.yahoo.com/config/send_webmesg?.target=miladymouse"><img src="http://opi.yahoo.com/online?u=miladymouse&amp;m=g&amp;t=0" alt="miladymouse" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="aim:goim?screenname=miladymouse&amp;message=Hi.+Are+you+there?"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/aim.gif" alt="miladymouse" border="0" /></a><br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=745"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1160.msg11613#msg11613"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1160.msg11613#msg11613">Re: Parents.. a little help plz..</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #40 on:</b> October 07, 2004, 06:16:33 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Dwalion, I know what you are saying now, but the common mistake in child raising is forgetting that each child is their own little individual self.  If every child acted the same way, it would be easy to pinpoint what is perceived to be abuse, but this is not the case.  It&#039;s ok to be vigilant and protective when it comes to children, just please make sure you have all the facts before accusing someone unjustly.  As far as being a mean SOB, there is a cure for that and it&#039;s called compassion.  <br /><br />Over the past ten years, I&#039;ve seen at least 50 children come into my house and no two were ever alike.  I used to think that abuse was based on a child&#039;s socio-economic background but that&#039;s not always the case, nor is the fact that just because a child shows signs of abuse that he/she is being abused.  I&#039;ve had several cases wherein the child claimed emotional abuse,  only to find out it was because his/her parents couldn&#039;t afford the &quot;luxury items&quot; that their friends had...cell phones, computers, cars, PS2&#039;s, etc. and they figured those items could be gained being placed in a foster home.  A child service agency will ALWAYS err on the side of caution, removing a child from the home first and then sorting out the details.  Those children weren&#039;t missing medical care, they were well-fed, clothed (perhaps not in the latest fashions but with hole and stain-free items), came from clean, loving environments, but that wasn&#039;t enough for them.  You should have seen the look on one 17 year old girl&#039;s face when told by her caseworker that if she wanted the &quot;luxuries&quot; she should get a job.  <br /><br />The black and blue bruises on one particular child sent to me turned out to be nothing more than this child&#039;s own clumsiness.  He&#039;d was always trying to walk and chew gum at the same time and it just wasn&#039;t working for him.  His parents were devastated when they removed him for suspected abuse.  I don&#039;t know how many times I&#039;d catch him reading a book while trying to navigate steps...he was just an accident waiting to happen and trying to get him to focus his attention at doing only one thing at a time was like talking to a brick wall.  <br /><br />But then there are those special cases where it tears your heart out seeing the abuse/neglect.  A 9-year old who daily stole food from the local convenience store to feed her younger siblings while her mother used their assistance check for drugs.  A 13-year old &quot;hooking&quot; so that she could buy the necessities to go to school while her mother said she was old enough to find a job and make her own way.  The children who are locked in an attic in 100+ degree heat without food or water or a way to get out just because they were &quot;annoying their parents by giggling while playing a game&quot;.  Those parents should be hung from the highest rafters and shown no mercy whatsoever!<br /><br />True abusers also will do everything in their power to hide their actions from law-abiding peeps.  They tend to keep to themselves, keep their children out of sight and that&#039;s why the abuse is so very hard to detect in children under school age. <br /> <br />Just by looking at Incy&#039;s mischievous little imp you can visually see that this little cutie is just being her normal baby self.  <br /><br />Keep on parenting with a loving and open heart, get to know other parents and always keep those lines of communication open...you just never know when one of your little ones will do something out of the ordinary that will make you tear your hair out one minute and laugh hysterically the next.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />Needaa Spiritfyter<br />Guild Leader, Dark Empire
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
